    "explanation": "Anduin excels on Maps that feature static Objectives where team fights do not last too long (such as Shrines on Dragon Shire). Choke points can make for great locations for Divine Star to get value from as well as to catch enemy Heroes with Lightbomb.\n\nAll in all, Anduin's well-rounded kit leaves him with no real Map vulnerabilities, except for a moderate disadvantage on Maps where the Objective takes too much time to be won that his Mana eventually expires (for example Braxis Holdout) and where there are good paths for flanking."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Lightwell Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "Anduin's Lightwell Build is all about keeping yourself and allied Heroes healthy over time, which is great when facing a team that mostly relies on sustain damage but weak against burst damage.\n\nTry to apply Renew at Level 16 on as many allied Heroes as possible, then rely on Moral Compass to refresh its duration from the distance every 5 seconds with either Divine Star or Basic Attacks.\n\nMost of the Talents in this Build will contribute to reducing the cooldown of Lightwell at Level 1, increasing your healing output without having to spend extra Mana but with the need for allied Heroes to stand in the healing area for a few seconds. For this reason, we find it better for stationary fights to control a given location on the battlefield.",
